      "english": "The next year, the emperor intended greatly to boast to the Hu of the abundance of birds and beasts; in autumn he ordered the governor of Right Fufeng to mobilize the people into the Southern Mountains, from Baoxie in the west to Hongnong in the east, driving south into Hanzhong, spreading nets and snares, capturing bears, wild boars, tigers, leopards, [missing graph], foxes, hares, and elk, loading them in cage-carts, and sending them to the Changyang Bear-Shooting Lodge."
